==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|Queen|-s-|-land}}, equivalent to ''Queen's Land'' and named in honour of [[w:Queen Victoria|Queen Victoria]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkwɪːnzˌlæːnd/|a=AusE}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Typheuss-Queensland.wav|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkwiːnz.lænd/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Queensland.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkwiːnzlənd/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-Us Queensland.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{place|en|One of the six <<states>> of <<c/Australia>>|capital=Brisbane}}. It occupies the north-eastern part of the continent.
# {{lb|en|historical}} The self-governing [[colony]] (1859—1901) of what is now the state of Queensland.

